# Weekly sync freeze

Friday UTC early-morning GitHub Actions rebuild brand catalogues (UK ~02:00 start).
A slower **older** Vercel build can overwrite a newer production deploy
(2026-08-17: London Undercover vs Chanel makeup).

## Before any `git push` to `main`, empty-commit redeploy, or `push-product-images-tag.py`

Run:

```bash
python3 scripts/weekly-sync-status.py
```

- Exit **0**: deploy as usual (`auto-deploy.mdc`).
- Exit **2**: **do not push**. Do not start a new catalogue import that you would then deploy.

**Exception:** If the user explicitly says to deploy now / ignore the freeze / ship despite weekly sync, push as requested.

## If the user asks for a new update while frozen

Do the work locally only if it stays unpushed, and reply in Korean that:

- 지금은 주간 동기화 요일/진행 중이라 새 업데이트를 배포하지 않는다
- 스크립트가 알려 준 남은 작업이 끝나면 이어서 배포하겠다

Do not ask “지금 강행할까요?”. Wait until `weekly-sync-status.py` exits 0, then deploy without being asked again if the original request is still in this chat.

## Schedule (UTC ≈ UK BST = UTC+1)

All brand syncs are **biweekly**: they fire every Friday but a `gate` job lets them run only on **odd ISO weeks**. Even weeks exit before any catalogue push, so they do not block deploys. Staggered from **01:00 UTC (02:00 UK / BST)**:

- banner 01:00, CW 02:00, GG 03:00, BB 04:00, AX 05:00, PR 06:00, BS 07:00, PS 08:00, LU 09:00, GC 10:00, CH 11:00, DI 12:00, CE 13:00, BV/VW 13:30, AL/YS 14:00, MB 14:30
- Keep the `gate` job when adding a new brand sync workflow.

## Vercel build cost — batched deploys

- Sync bots commit through `scripts/ci-commit-push.sh`, which appends `[catalog-sync]`. `scripts/vercel-skip-stale.sh` skips Vercel builds for those commits.
- `.github/workflows/catalog-deploy.yml` (hourly) pushes one empty `chore: deploy catalogue sync batch` commit when main HEAD is still a `[catalog-sync]` commit and no sync/scrape workflow is queued or running (odd-week Fridays: not before 16:00 UTC). Result: one Vercel build per sync batch instead of one per brand.
- New bot workflows that push catalogue data must use `ci-commit-push.sh` (or include `[catalog-sync]`). Never put `[catalog-sync]` on human/agent code commits — they would not deploy until the next batch run.
